1. What is Computer Networking?
Computer networking is the process of connecting two or more computers or devices to share data, resources, and information.

Benefits:
-Resource sharing
-File sharing
-Communication
-Internet access
-Centralized data management

2. Types of Networks
PAN-Personal Area Network	(Small network around one person)
LAN-Local Area Network	(Network within a home, office, or building)
MAN-Metropolitan Area (Network	Covers a city)
WAN-Wide Area Network	(Covers large geographical areas)
